 75ZN c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2017Wr01:                          
 75ZN2c  Phys Lett B771, 385 (2017).                                            
 75ZN c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster); June 22, 2017                         
 75ZN c  2017Wr01: E(p)=1.4 GeV incident on UC{-x} target at ISOLDE-CERN        
 75ZN2c  facility. The {+75}Zn nuclei were resonantly ionized using a resonant  
 75ZN3c  laser-ion source, accelerated to 30 keV, and separated by              
 75ZN4c  high-resolution separator. The ions were cooled using a gas-filled     
 75ZN5c  radio-frequency quadrupole (RFQ-ISCOOL). Measured hyperfine spectra    
 75ZN6c  using collinear laser spectroscopy using COLLAPS setup at ISOLDE-CERN. 
 75ZN7c  Deduced spins, |m, Q, isomer. Comparison with large-scale shell model  
 75ZN8c  calculations                                                           
 75ZN c  For the calibration of nuclear moments, |m=+0.875479 {I9} from         
 75ZN2c  literature and Q=+0.122 {I10} (2017Wr01) for the stable {+67}Zn nuclide
 75ZN3c  were used as references                                                
